# ============================================
# Dynamic Action Panel — environment
# ============================================
#
# There is nothing to configure here any more, and that is deliberate.
#
# Deployment used to read VAULT_PATH from a .env file, which meant an invisible,
# machine-local, Dropbox-synced value decided which Obsidian vault got written
# to — including by `npm run build`, which deployed as a side effect. A stale
# value from another machine was enough to aim a destructive copy at a
# productive vault.
#
# Deploy targets are now project configuration, in:
#
#   scripts/deployCore.mjs  ->  DEPLOY_TARGETS
#
# Two named targets exist, `smoke` and `prod`, and a deployment refuses any
# path that is not exactly one of them. Changing where the plugin installs is
# therefore a visible, reviewable edit rather than a hidden variable.
#
# Commands:
#
#   npm run build         build only, touches no vault
#   npm run deploy:smoke  install into the disposable smoke vault
#   npm run deploy:prod   install into the productive vault
#   npm run dev           watch build, touches no vault
#   npm run dev:smoke     watch build that also installs into the smoke vault
#
# VAULT_PATH is no longer read by anything. If you still have it in a .env file
# it is inert; you can delete the file.
